class.description:
[RenderEffectSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"render_effect"[/code]. It stores two kinds of values for the player, and every value takes effect at once:
- [b]Effect quality:[/b] the global quality of SSAO, SSIL, SDFGI, [VoxelGI], volumetric fog, subsurface scattering and depth of field, pushed to [RenderingServer] ([method RenderingServer.environment_set_ssao_quality], [method RenderingServer.environment_set_ssil_quality], [method RenderingServer.environment_set_sdfgi_ray_count], [method RenderingServer.voxel_gi_set_quality], [method RenderingServer.environment_set_volumetric_fog_volume_size], [method RenderingServer.sub_surface_scattering_set_quality], [method RenderingServer.camera_attributes_set_dof_blur_quality] and the others). The defaults are the matching project settings.
- [b]Environment overrides:[/b] switches that turn glow, SSAO, SSIL, screen-space reflections, fog or volumetric fog off in every [Environment] ([code]allow_*[/code]), and brightness, contrast and saturation that multiply the adjustment of every environment. They are applied at render time ([method RenderingServer.environment_set_global_effect_disabled], [method RenderingServer.environment_set_global_adjustment]): the [Environment] resources keep the values the level author set, environments of scenes loaded later are covered too, and turning a switch on again restores the authored value. An environment whose author did not enable adjustments counts as [code]1.0[/code]; the adjustment pass runs for it only while a value differs from [code]1.0[/code].
The settings resource is a [RenderEffectSettings]; the file is [code]user://settings/render_effect.ini[/code] by default, in the format of [member ProjectSettings.settings/general/default_format] (or of its domain group [code]settings/<domain>/[/code]). If it does not exist yet, the file of the former domain name ([code]user://settings/video_effect.ini[/code]) is read once at startup and written under the new name; the old file is kept. When the game starts, the stored values are applied in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SERVERS], after the renderer has read the project settings.
[b]Exclusions:[/b] the environment of a [WorldEnvironment] or [Camera3D] in the group [method get_ignore_group] ([code]ignore_quality_settings[/code]) is not affected by the overrides; [method set_environment_ignored] does the same from code.
[b]Renderers:[/b] SSAO, SSIL, SDFGI, screen-space reflections, volumetric fog and subsurface scattering exist in the Forward+ renderer only; [VoxelGI] and depth of field in Forward+ and Mobile. Glow, fog and the adjustments work in every renderer, also in the Compatibility renderer (default in the Web export). [method SettingsServer.is_value_supported] returns [code]false[/code] for values the current renderer ignores and [method get_unsupported_setting_names] lists them, so that a settings menu can hide them. Such values are still stored, but not pushed; a warning names them once.
Values out of range are clamped with a warning (for example [code]ssao_adaptive_target[/code] [code]0[/code] to [code]1[/code], [code]volumetric_fog_volume_size[/code] [code]16[/code] to [code]512[/code], [code]brightness[/code] [code]0.01[/code] to [code]8[/code]). An enum value out of range is replaced by the default.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	$SsaoQuality.selected = RenderEffectSettingsServer.get_ssao_quality()
	$Reflections.button_pressed = RenderEffectSettingsServer.is_ssr_allowed()
	$Reflections.visible = RenderEffectSettingsServer.is_value_supported(&"allow_ssr")

func _on_reflections_toggled(pressed):
	RenderEffectSettingsServer.set_allow_ssr(pressed)

func _on_brightness_value_changed(value):
	RenderEffectSettingsServer.set_brightness(value)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    GetNode<OptionButton>("SsaoQuality").Selected = (int)RenderEffectSettingsServer.GetSsaoQuality();
    GetNode<CheckBox>("Reflections").ButtonPressed = RenderEffectSettingsServer.IsSsrAllowed();
    // Methods of the base class are called through Singleton.
    GetNode<CheckBox>("Reflections").Visible = RenderEffectSettingsServer.Singleton.IsValueSupported("allow_ssr");
}

private void OnReflectionsToggled(bool pressed)
{
    RenderEffectSettingsServer.SetAllowSsr(pressed);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] In C#, the static class [code skip-lint]RenderEffectSettingsServer[/code] only has the methods of this class. The methods of [SettingsServer] are called through [code]RenderEffectSettingsServer.Singleton[/code].
